# Frontend Module Layout

Prefer `Frontend/src/modules/<module-name>/` for all new work.

```txt
modules/<module-name>/
  pages/       # route entry screens (thin)
  components/  # UI only, no API transport
  hooks/       # orchestration and screen logic
  services/    # API/http calls only
  constants/   # maps/options/static values
  utils/       # pure helpers
  store/       # optional state slice/query
  schemas/     # optional validation schemas
  index.js     # barrel export
```

## Architecture Rules

- `pages/` compose `hooks/` + `components/`; keep them small.
- `components/` must not call `fetch`/`apiClient` directly.
- `hooks/` coordinate UI state + service calls.
- `services/` are side-effect/data access layer only.
- Move code to `shared/` only when reused by 2+ modules.

## Naming

- Use lowercase folder names: `components`, `hooks`, `services`, `pages`, `utils`, `constants`.
- Hooks: `useXxx.js` or `useXxxController.js`.
- Services: `xxxService.js`.
- Pages: `XxxPage.jsx`.

## Security Baseline

- Never trust auth/role from `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
- Sanitize rendered rich HTML via `@shared/security/sanitizeHtml`.
